<main class="immersion-builder" aria-label="RIST ImmersionBuilder">
 <header>
  <p>RIST STUDIO</p>
  <h1>IMMERSIONBUILDER</h1>
  <span>Design how a world is experienced without changing the world itself.</span>
 </header>

 <section class="immersion-intro">
  <strong>IMMERSION PROFILE</strong>
  <p>ImmersionBuilder will read the current World ID and world coordinates, then attach presentation and device-experience settings without redefining terrain, regions, tiers, layers, objects, or spatial identity.</p>
 </section>

 <section class="immersion-grid" aria-label="ImmersionBuilder planned systems">
  <article><span>◫</span><div><strong>PARALLAX</strong><p>Build visual depth from the world's existing tier, layer, and Z coordinates. This will become the first functional ImmersionBuilder module.</p></div><small>FIRST BUILD</small></article>
  <article><span>⌖</span><div><strong>AUGMENTED REALITY</strong><p>Anchor compatible world content into physical space while preserving the same world identity and scale.</p></div><small>PLANNED</small></article>
  <article><span>◉</span><div><strong>SPATIAL AUDIO</strong><p>Place ambience, voices, effects, and environmental sound within world space using distance and direction.</p></div><small>PLANNED</small></article>
  <article><span>✧</span><div><strong>HIGH RESOLUTION ASSETS</strong><p>Select higher-detail representations for capable devices and close viewing without changing the underlying asset identity.</p></div><small>PLANNED</small></article>
  <article><span>≋</span><div><strong>HAPTIC FEEDBACK</strong><p>Translate boundaries, materials, events, and accessibility cues into supported touch and controller feedback.</p></div><small>PLANNED</small></article>
 </section>

 <section class="immersion-rule">
  <strong>AUTHORITY RULE</strong>
  <p>ImmersionBuilder may read World ID, regions, coordinates, tiers, layers, objects, and events. It may never redefine them. WorldBuilder owns what exists; ImmersionBuilder owns how it is experienced.</p>
 </section>
</main>

